Copied under internal/upstream at the revision above:
  relay, mux, obfs, credpool, provider, provider/static, exit.

Local changes:
  import paths now use github.com/sagernet/sing-box/protocol/turnrelay/internal/upstream.
  relay uses pion/transport/v5/stdnet to match the pinned pion/turn v5.1.3.
  relay dials through the sing-box dialer first, so the TURN hostname is resolved
  by the core resolver and the socket obeys detour and bind options. Abstract
  detour sockets use a numeric peer identifier to avoid a second DNS lookup.
  mux counts authenticated inbound frames so the adapter can replace a stale
  session after complete silence. The exit bounds idle allocation reads with
  its ZombieAfter timeout; the patched mux/server.go also builds unchanged in
  the pinned upstream server checkout.
  provider/vk, app, tray, cmd, and the upstream singbox adapter are not copied.
  the outbound exposes static credentials with exit only, srtp or dtls obfs,
  and requires the server certificate SHA-256; wrap is not exposed.
